{
 "brief": "Khulud Faraj Allah, a widow and mother of three in Gaza, has converted her tent into a sweets and pastries kiosk to support her family, Shehab Wire reported. The enterprise represents one response to conditions in the enclave where women now head approximately one quarter of all households.\n\nThe transformation of her shelter into a small business reflects the economic pressures facing displaced families across Gaza, where survival often requires improvisation and multiple income strategies among vulnerable populations.",
